---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy | Somnori';
const description = 'Privacy information for the Somnori pre-release website.';
const alternates = [
  { lang: 'en', href: '/privacy' },
  { lang: 'ru', href: '/ru/privacy' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/privacy" type="article" locale="en" alternates={alternates}>
  <section class="article-hero">
    <div class="article-shell">
      <div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Somnori</a> / Privacy</div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy at Somnori</h1>
      <p class="lead">Night thoughts, voice recordings and dream data can be unusually personal. This page describes the current pre-release website; the Android app will receive a separate, implementation-specific privacy policy before public distribution.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <article class="article-shell prose section-tight">
    <h2>This website today</h2>
    <p>The initial Somnori website is a static informational site. It does not currently provide user accounts, accept night recordings or dream uploads, or offer a web dream-interpreter form.</p>
    <p>Like most websites, the hosting infrastructure may process ordinary technical request data such as IP address, browser information, requested URL and timestamps for security and server operation.</p>

    <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
    <p>No advertising analytics integration is included in the initial source build. If analytics, consent tools or other tracking technologies are added later, this page will be updated before they are relied on in production.</p>

    <h2>The Android app</h2>
    <p>The app can contain voice recordings, night thoughts and dream-journal information. Before the public Android release, Somnori will publish a separate policy that states exactly what is stored on-device, what—if anything—is transmitted to external services, how transcription works, and which export or delete controls actually exist.</p>
    <p>We will not use future product intentions as present-tense privacy promises.</p>

    <h2>Sensitive night data</h2>
    <p>Thoughts, voice notes and dreams can contain intimate material. Specific claims about encryption, cloud storage or fully local processing will therefore only be made when they are verified in the corresponding shipped build.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>This page will change as the public product and website capabilities change. Material changes should be reflected here alongside the relevant product release.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
